BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cookie Queens
DTSTART:20260517T180000Z
DTEND:20260517T194500Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T180000Z
UID:vM6A4LaGs2
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 91 mins (1h31m)\n\nThis charming SXSW Film & TV Fest
 ival Audience Award-winning documentary profiles four resolute girls throu
 gh Girl Scout Cookie season as they find their place in the $800 million p
 henomenon.Executive Producer Steve Hall and Co-Producer Ann Rogers schedul
 ed to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/cookie-queens\n\nEstimated 
 start: 11:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lady
DTSTART:20260517T183000Z
DTEND:20260517T201500Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T183000Z
UID:k5MH3V8ik0
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 95 mins (1h35m)\n\nIn this absurdly hilarious mockum
 entary\, a young filmmaker agrees to film the behind-the-scenes vanity pro
 ject of the obnoxiously entitled Lady Isabella\, only for something unseen
  and quite strange to happen.Director Samuel Abrahams scheduled to attend 
 the May 16 screening.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/lady\n\nEstimated s
 tart: 11:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Strange River
DTSTART:20260517T184500Z
DTEND:20260517T204500Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T184500Z
UID:vCKCOxUY6h
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 106 mins (1h46m)\n\nSixteen-year-old Dídac spends a
  summer cycling along the Danube with his family. When a mysterious boy ap
 pears\, new emotions stir\, subtly shifting family dynamics and guiding D
 ídac through a transformative journey of first love and self-discovery. T
 his film is generously sponsored by Jeff Stolz & Tim O'Connor.\n\nhttps://
 www.siff.net/festival/strange-river\n\nEstimated start: 11:55
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Aanikoobijigan [ancestor/great-grandparent/great-grandchild]
DTSTART:20260517T190000Z
DTEND:20260517T204500Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T190000Z
UID:EXUo8ElEbw
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 93 mins (1h33m)\n\nIndigenous elders and activists f
 ighting to reclaim ancestors’ remains\, exposing colonial violence and i
 nstitutional resistance while affirming that returning bodies to the earth
  restores dignity\, memory\, and balance.Director Zack Khalil (Ojibway) sc
 heduled to attend May 16 screening.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/aanik
 oobijigan-ancestor/great-grandparent/great-grandchild\n\nEstimated start: 
 12:10
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Prisoners of the Earth (1939)
DTSTART:20260517T203000Z
DTEND:20260517T221000Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T203000Z
UID:34eG8ty9KR
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 86 mins (1h26m)\n\nThe most acclaimed film by one of
  classic Argentine cinema’s foremost directors is a gut-punching work of
  social realism: a group of desperate men are conscripted to labor on a tr
 eacherous plantation—a situation that boils over in an explosive act of 
 rebellion.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/prisoners-of-the-earth\n\nEsti
 mated start: 13:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rising Through the Fray
DTSTART:20260517T203000Z
DTEND:20260517T221000Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T203000Z
UID:bvBXKq3yv2
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 88 mins (1h28m)\n\nRoller derby built its identity o
 n the outsider. Indigenous Rising is what it looks like when over 30 Indig
 enous Nations lace up together\, skate onto the track under their own bann
 er\, and refuse to be invisible.Director Courtney Montour scheduled to att
 end.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/rising-through-the-fray\n\nEstimated
  start: 13:40
LOCATION:PACCAR IMAX Theater at Pacific Science Center\, None
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Big Cheese
DTSTART:20260517T203000Z
DTEND:20260517T222500Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T203000Z
UID:KW868SHcr1
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 101 mins (1h41m)\n\nAdam “Mr. Moo” Moskowitz is 
 on a mission to make the world take American cheesemongers seriously. For 
 over a decade\, he’s led a team of eccentric misfits to the Olympics of 
 Cheese\, where Team USA has never won. Could this be their year? Director 
 Sara Joe Wolansky and Subjects Courtney Johnson & Adam Moskowitz schedul
 ed to attend. After the film on Sat\, May 16\, pass and ticket-holders ca
 n head over to Tin Lizzie for an udderly delicious cheese tasting\, courte
 sy of Street Cheese and Peterson Cheese\, with custom wine pairings availa
 ble for purchase. It will surely stink. Wink.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/fest
 ival/the-big-cheese\n\nEstimated start: 13:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Phoenix Jones: The Rise and Fall of a Real Life Superhero
DTSTART:20260517T210000Z
DTEND:20260517T231000Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T210000Z
UID:9uabpNndG1
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 116 mins (1h56m)\n\nReal-life superhero\, or untrain
 ed vigilante? A new documentary revisits the Phoenix Jones saga\, a fascin
 ating chapter in recent Seattle history\, with never-before-seen footage a
 nd illuminating interviews with Phoenix’s family\, co-superheroes\, and 
 enemies. Director Bayan Joonam\, Producer Claire Chubbuck\, Producer/Edito
 r Duncan Dickerson\, and Subject Phoenix Jones scheduled to attend.\n\nhtt
 ps://www.siff.net/festival/phoenix-jones-the-rise-and-fall-of-a-real-life-
 superhero\n\nEstimated start: 14:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Body Blow
DTSTART:20260517T211500Z
DTEND:20260517T230500Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T211500Z
UID:1Xg0cXIrg5
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 99 mins (1h39m)\n\nDanger and desire go hand-in-hand
  as a musclebound young cop goes undercover in Sydney’s gay scene\, only
  to fall for an alluring twink fatale\, in Dean Francis’ explicit and ca
 mpy neo-noir that refracts the erotic thriller through an unapologetically
  queer lens.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/body-blow\n\nEstimated start
 : 14:25
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Black Burns Fast
DTSTART:20260517T213000Z
DTEND:20260517T232000Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T213000Z
UID:w5MqVamC0o
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 96 mins (1h36m)\n\nAt an elite South African boardin
 g school\, scholarship student Luthando has mastered the art of invisibili
 ty until the arrival of free-spirited Ayanda upends her straight-laced exi
 stence.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/black-burns-fast\n\nEstimated sta
 rt: 14:40
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beat the Lotto
DTSTART:20260517T230000Z
DTEND:20260518T004000Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T230000Z
UID:LpwqIfhvgJ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 89 mins (1h29m)\n\nWhen Ireland inaugurated its Nati
 onal Lottery\, it became a national obsession. One man soon discovered a f
 law in the system\, gaming the odds to win it all and dividing the nation 
 in the process.Director Ross Whitaker scheduled to attend May 17 screening
 .Supported by Culture Ireland.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/beat-the-l
 otto\n\nEstimated start: 16:10
LOCATION:PACCAR IMAX Theater at Pacific Science Center\, None
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sundays
DTSTART:20260517T230000Z
DTEND:20260518T011000Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T230000Z
UID:9gKSXh34CY
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 117 mins (1h57m)\n\nAt 17\, Ainara faces a life-chan
 ging choice: after high school\, she considers becoming a nun. Her decisio
 n unsettles her family\, especially her aunt Montse\, who fears it means l
 osing freedom. The year's Goya Award standout offers a stirring tale about
  the fragile balance between faith and skepticism.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net
 /festival/sundays\n\nEstimated start: 16:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Love Chaos Kin
DTSTART:20260517T231500Z
DTEND:20260518T010500Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T231500Z
UID:85qO1ybSAD
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 98 mins (1h38m)\n\nAn Indian immigrant couple adopts
  twins of Navajo descent and stays connected to the biological family. Lov
 e Chaos Kin is a clear-eyed look at what belonging to more than one world 
 actually means. Director Chithra Jeyaram scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://w
 ww.siff.net/festival/love-chaos-kin\n\nEstimated start: 16:25
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Powwow People
DTSTART:20260517T233000Z
DTEND:20260518T013000Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T233000Z
UID:tsHWChiaRM
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 106 mins (1h46m)\n\nPowwow People immerses us in a s
 ingle day at a powwow\, guided by Reuben Little Head’s humor and heart\,
  culminating in a long take honoring community as privilege. Director Sky 
 Hopinka (Ho-Chunk Nation/Pechanga Band of Luiseño Indians) and Impact Pro
 ducer Amber Morning Star Byars scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.ne
 t/festival/powwow-people\n\nEstimated start: 16:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Balandrau\, Where the Fierce Wind Blew
DTSTART:20260518T000000Z
DTEND:20260518T021500Z
DTSTAMP:20260518T000000Z
UID:RpixdHlAr8
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 116 mins (1h56m)\n\nOn December 30\, 2000\, friends 
 climbing Mount Balandrau in the Catalan Pyrenees get caught in a sudden\, 
 savage blizzard. Visibility vanishes\, winds roar\, and survival becomes a
  desperate fight against one of the mountain’s deadliest storms. Produce
 r Guille Cascante scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/ba
 landrau-where-the-fierce-wind-blew\n\nEstimated start: 17:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Birds of War
DTSTART:20260518T000000Z
DTEND:20260518T014000Z
DTSTAMP:20260518T000000Z
UID:n7br5DOGYw
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 85 mins (1h25m)\n\nLebanese journalist Janay Boulos 
 and Syrian activist and cameraman Abd Alkader Habak share their extraordin
 ary love story\, told through 13 years of personal archives spanning revol
 utions\, war\, and exile. Director Janay Boulos scheduled to attend. This 
 film is generously sponsored by Katherine & David De Bruyn.\n\nhttps://www
 .siff.net/festival/birds-of-war\n\nEstimated start: 17:15
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Happy Birthday
DTSTART:20260518T013000Z
DTEND:20260518T032000Z
DTSTAMP:20260518T013000Z
UID:KSEMPwFxok
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 92 mins (1h32m)\n\nEight-year-old Toha has big plans
 \; she wants to throw her friend Nelly a birthday party. But the differenc
 es between them will make this a challenge in ways she may not fully under
 stand. This film is generously sponsored by Xixi & Jonathan Shakes.\n\nhtt
 ps://www.siff.net/festival/happy-birthday\n\nEstimated start: 18:45
LOCATION:PACCAR IMAX Theater at Pacific Science Center\, None
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Edie Arnold is a Loser
DTSTART:20260518T020000Z
DTEND:20260518T034500Z
DTSTAMP:20260518T020000Z
UID:HhSTxWytqr
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 87 mins (1h27m)\n\nLace up your combat boots and whi
 p out that black eyeliner for Edie Arnold is a Loser\, an infectiously cha
 rming coming-of-age flick about a self-proclaimed loser starting a punk ba
 nd at her Catholic high school. Directors Kade Atwood and Megan Rico sched
 uled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/edie-arnold-is-a-loser\n\
 nEstimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Invite
DTSTART:20260518T020000Z
DTEND:20260518T040500Z
DTSTAMP:20260518T020000Z
UID:g2wD31Ftqe
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 107 mins (1h47m)\n\nJoe and Angela’s marriage is o
 n thin ice. When they invite their enigmatic upstairs neighbors for a dinn
 er party\, the night spirals into unexpected places. Have they reignited t
 he spark or lit the match that burns it all down? Director & star Olivia 
 Wilde scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-invite\n\n
 Estimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Furious
DTSTART:20260518T024500Z
DTEND:20260518T045500Z
DTSTAMP:20260518T024500Z
UID:lgcftBKvHW
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 113 mins (1h53m)\n\nAfter the daughter of Wang Wei (
 Xie Miao) is kidnapped by a criminal network and he receives no help from 
 the corrupt police\, Wei sets out on a rampage to find her himself. His on
 ly ally is Navin (Joe Taslim) – a relentless journalist whose wife has m
 ysteriously disappeared. Fueled by a furious vengeance\, the unlikely duo 
 ruthlessly fights against the kidnappers in this explosive martial arts sh
 owdown.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-furious\n\nEstimated start: 2
 0:00
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:RADIOHEART: The Drive and Times of DJ Kevin Cole
DTSTART:20260518T030000Z
DTEND:20260518T044000Z
DTSTAMP:20260518T030000Z
UID:kvibpJeXnB
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 83 mins (1h23m)\n\nIn his 25-year tenure at KEXP\, D
 J Kevin Cole helped define not just who Seattle listens to\, but how we li
 sten\, fostering delight and curiosity with every recommendation. RADIOHEA
 RT\, a bio-doc about Cole’s remarkable life\, boasts a killer soundtrack
 \, a wealth of nostalgic archival footage\, and cameos from Seattle musica
 l legends.Directors Peter Hilgendorf and Andrew Franks\, plus Producer Reb
 ecca Staffel and Subject Kevin Cole scheduled to attend.This film is gener
 ously sponsored by David Prokopy.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/radiohe
 art-the-drive-and-times-of-dj-kevin-cole\n\nEstimated start: 20:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Friend’s House is Here
DTSTART:20260518T030000Z
DTEND:20260518T045000Z
DTSTAMP:20260518T030000Z
UID:XqO45sEkBn
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 95 mins (1h35m)\n\nPari and Hanna are best friends a
 nd active participants in Tehran’s vibrant underground arts scene. But t
 he risk of running afoul of the government is omnipresent\, forcing diffic
 ult decisions.Director Hossein Keshavarz and Maryam Ataei scheduled to att
 end.  This film is generously sponsored by Lynn Dissinger.\n\nhttps://www.
 siff.net/festival/the-friends-house-is-here\n\nEstimated start: 20:15
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
